{
  "bio_paragraph_1": "Meghan Clarisse is a Colorado-based singer-songwriter delivering “music with country roots and cowgirl boots.” With a voice as grounded as the Mountain West she calls home, Meghan blends Americana, country and rock into heartfelt songs that tell stories of resilience, family, and wide-open landscapes.",
  "bio_paragraph_2": "Meghan and her band perform across the front range playing bars, venues, and festivals such as Lakewood’s Cider Days, Parker Days, and the Adams County Fair. Her discography includes Songs from the Sofa (2023), the collaborative EP Kindred Spirits (2024), and her full-length album Shadows of a Ghost Town (2025), an evocative exploration of death, nature, and the soul of the West.",
  "bio_paragraph_3": "Off-stage, she volunteers with Musicians on Call, bringing live music to patients at Children’s Hospital and the VA in Denver. With every song and show, she builds community, lifts up fellow artists, and reminds audiences why music matters.",
  "pull_quote": "Music with country roots and cowgirl boots.",
